      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "The Hub keeps the Anthropic API key out of its own process environment through **credential scoping** \u2014 according to [[credential-scoping]]:\n\n1. **The key is never stored in the Hub\u0027s environment**: A local secrets loader reads the Anthropic API key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup, but does not add it to the Hub\u0027s own process environment variables.\n\n2. **Injection only into child processes**: The key is injected only into the environment of spawned child processes (the Ingest and Query agents) immediately before those processes start.\n\n3. **Security isolation**: This design prevents a compromised or misbehaving Hub process from leaking the credential simply by inspecting its own environment variables \u2014 the key exists only in the short-lived child processes that actually call the Anthropic API.\n\nThis approach keeps credential exposure surface minimal and temporally scoped to only the processes that actually need it.",
